Let's dive into the code in `HomeView.jsx`.

**Overview:**

The `HomeView` component is a functional component that receives several props from its parent component, `ManagerDashboard`. It uses these props to display a user's performance overview, including their average score, total users, total assessments, and recent exams.

**Props:**

The `HomeView` component receives the following props:

* `managerName`: The name of the manager.
* `timeOfDay`: A string indicating the time of day (e.g., "Good morning", "Good afternoon", etc.).
* `averageScore`: The average score of the users.
* `totalUsers`: The total number of users.
* `totalAssessments`: The total number of assessments.
* `recentExams`: An array of recent exams.
* `currentPage`: The current page number.
* `totalPages`: The total number of pages.
* `pageInput`: The current page input value.
* `handlePreviousPage`: A function to handle previous page navigation.
* `handleNextPage`: A function to handle next page navigation.
* `handlePageInputChange`: A function to handle page input changes.
* `handlePageSubmit`: A function to handle page submit.

**Code:**

Here's the code for the `HomeView` component:
```jsx
const HomeView = ({
  managerName,
  timeOfDay,
  averageScore,
  totalUsers,
  totalAssessments,
  recentExams,
  currentPage,
  totalPages,
  pageInput,
  handlePreviousPage,
  handleNextPage,
  handlePageInputChange,
  handlePageSubmit,
}) => {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2 className="text-2xl font-bold text-red-900">Welcome, {managerName}</h2>
      <p className="text-gray-500 mt-2 mb-6">{timeOfDay}! Here's Users performance overview.</p>

      <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-8">
        <div className="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border-l-4 border-blue-500">
          <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Average Score</h3>
          <p className="text-3xl font-bold text-blue-600">{averageScore}%</p>
          <p className="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2">Across all assessments</p>
        </div>
        <div className="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border-l-4 border-green-500">
          <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Total Users</h3>
          <p className="text-3xl font-bold text-green-600">{totalUsers}</p>
          <p className="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2">Total No. of users available</p>
        </div>
        <div className="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border-l-4 border-violet-500">
          <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Total Assessments</h3>
          <p className="text-3xl font-bold text-violet-600">{totalAssessments}</p>
          <p className="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2">Unique exams available</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div className="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 mb-8">
        <h3 className="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Recent Exams</h3>
        <RecentExamsTable
          recentExams={recentExams}
          currentPage={currentPage}
          totalPages={totalPages}
          pageInput={pageInput}
          handlePreviousPage={handlePreviousPage}
          handleNextPage={handleNextPage}
          handlePageInputChange={handlePageInputChange}
          handlePageSubmit={handlePageSubmit}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};
```
**Explanation:**

The `HomeView` component uses a combination of HTML and CSS to display the user's performance overview. It uses the `grid` layout to display three columns of data: average score, total users, and total assessments.

The component also renders a `RecentExamsTable` component, which is a reusable component that displays a table of recent exams. The `RecentExamsTable` component receives several props from the `HomeView` component, including the recent exams data, current page number, total pages, and page input value.

The `HomeView` component uses the `handlePreviousPage`, `handleNextPage`, `handlePageInputChange`, and `handlePageSubmit` functions to handle pagination and page input changes. These functions are passed as props from the parent component, `ManagerDashboard`.

Overall, the `HomeView` component provides a concise and informative overview of the˙0

