The `pageInput` prop is used to display the current page number in the pagination component. It's also used to handle page input changes, allowing the user to navigate to a specific page by entering the page number.

Here's how it works:

1. The `pageInput` prop is passed from the parent component, `ManagerDashboard`, to the `HomeView` component.
2. The `HomeView` component renders a pagination component, which includes a text input field to enter the page number.
3. When the user enters a page number in the text input field, the `handlePageInputChange` function is called, which updates the `pageInput` prop with the new value.
4. The `pageInput` prop is then passed to the `RecentExamsTable` component, which uses it to display the correct page of data.
5. When the user submits the page input (e.g., by pressing Enter), the `handlePageSubmit` function is called, which navigates to the specified page.

By using the `pageInput` prop, the `HomeView` component can provide a seamless pagination experience, allowing users to easily navigate between pages.

Here's an example of how the `pageInput` prop is used in the `HomeView` component:
```jsx
<div className="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 mb-8">
  <h3 className="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Recent Exams</h3>
  <RecentExamsTable
    recentExams={recentExams}
    currentPage={currentPage}
    totalPages={totalPages}
    pageInput={pageInput}
    handlePreviousPage={handlePreviousPage}
    handleNextPage={handleNextPage}
    handlePageInputChange={handlePageInputChange}
    handlePageSubmit={handlePageSubmit}
  />
  <input
    type="number"
    value={pageInput}
    onChange={handlePageInputChange}
    className="w-full p-2 pl-10 text-sm text-gray-700 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-gray-600"
  />
  <button
    type="submit"
    onClick={handlePageSubmit}
    className="bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-bold py-2 px-4 rounded-lg"
  >
    Go
  </button>
</div>
```
In this example, the `pageInput` prop is used to display the current page number in the text input field, and to handle page input changes when the user enters a new page number. When the user submits the page input, the `handlePageSubmit` function is called, which navigates to the specified page.»

