This is a JavaScript code snippet that defines a React component. Here's a breakdown of what's happening:



**HTML Structure**

* The code defines a `div` element that contains two child elements:
	+ A `div` element with a class name of `flex justify-between items-center mb-4`
	+ A `button` element



**First `div` Element**

* The first `div` element has a class name of `flex justify-between items-center mb-4`, which suggests that it is a container element that uses Flexbox to layout its child elements.
* The class names can be broken down as follows:
	+ `flex`: enables Flexbox layout
	+ `justify-between`: justifies the child elements to the start and end of the container, with equal space between them
	+ `items-center`: centers the child elements vertically
	+ `mb-4`: adds a margin bottom of 4 units ( likely pixels or rem)
* The `div` element contains two child elements:
	+ An `h3` element with a class name of `text-xl font-semibold`
	+ A `button` element



**`h3` Element**

* The `h3` element has a class name of `text-xl font-semibold`, which suggests that it is a heading element with a large font size and a bold font weight.
* The class names can be broken down as follows:
	+ `text-xl`: sets the font size to extra large
	+ `font-semibold`: sets the font weight to semi-bold
* The `h3` element displays a text string that depends on the value of the `editingExamId` variable:
	+ If `editingExamId` is truthy, the text string is "Edit Exam Questions"
	+ If `editingExamId` is falsy, the text string is "Upload Exam Questions"



**`button` Element**

* The `button` element has an `onClick` event handler that calls the `toggleUploadedExams` function when the button is clicked.
* The `button` element has a class name of `bg-blue-500 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded hover:bg-blue-700`, which suggests that it is a blue button with white text and a rounded shape.
* The class names can be broken down as follows:
	+ `bg-blue-500`: sets the background color to a blue color with a medium lightness
	+ `text-white`: sets the text color to white
	+ `px-4`: adds a padding of 4 units ( likely pixels or rem) to the left and right sides of the button
	+ `py-2`: adds a padding of 2 units ( likely pixels or rem) to the top and bottom sides of the button
	+ `rounded`: adds a rounded shape to the button
	+ `hover:bg-blue-700`: changes the background color to a darker blue color when the button is hovered over
* The `button` element displays a text string that depends on the value of the `showUploadedExams` variable:
	+ If `showUploadedExams` is truthy, the text string is "Back to Upload"
	+ If `showUploadedExams` is falsy, the text string is "View Uploaded Exams"ˇ

